      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">a polypropylene that can be used as the polyolefin (A)</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">is preferably a homopolymer, and may be a copolymer, such as a block polymer, obtained by copolymerizing a comonomer other than propylene, such as an  ⁇ -olefin comonomer.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0091">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the lower limit of the amount of propylene structure included as a repeating unit in the polypropylene</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">may be, for example, 70 mol % or greater, 80 mol % or greater, 90 mol % or greater, 95 mol % or greater, or 99 mol % or greater.</span>
